Priority: optional
Maintainer: Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms, dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/peyton-howe/ubuntu-image-builder

Package: rk3588-aic8800-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms, aic8800-firmware
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-virtual | linux-headers-arm64
Description: DKMS driver and firmware for the AIC8800 USB Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module
 Out-of-tree driver for the Aicsemi AIC8800D80 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth module
 (USB) on the Radxa ROCK 5C, which the mainline kernel has no driver for.
 The source is radxa-pkg/aic8800 with its kernel 7.x build fixes applied
 (see README.md). The firmware comes from Radxa's aic8800-firmware package,
 which the image build downloads (scripts/fetch-aic8800-firmware.sh).
 .
 Headers are only recommended: the image build installs headers matching
 each installed kernel.
